Cross-reference: I have published the stage-by-stage numerical correctness assessment as a **separate documentation-only PR #256**.

**[Read the illustrated review](https://github.com/KingAlejandro/MotionCorr-standalone/blob/4731f46fbb73f1a7decb871267f37e35632c5a4f/docs/post_rc0/numerical_correctness_audit/README.md)**. It contains three SVG evidence charts and two Mermaid diagrams, with pinned source links and no Notion references.

The review separates:
- confirmed same-input CUDA peak-curvature loss and invalid C2R representation from routine FFTW/cuFFT roundoff;
- the observed near-tie/acceptance/fit amplification from unproven complete causal attribution;
- separately actionable inherited and CUDA-specific issues (boundary peak extrapolation, wrong model-guard domain, border interpolation, EER gain semantics, STAR precision);
- proposed native ablations and scientific-outcome gates from **experiments not yet run**.

PR #256 changes documentation only; it neither modifies production kernels nor proposes closing S1/S1.4 on the present evidence.
